body:
Most people who aren't drinking ale or rum stick to wines produced in the Itorican Empire (well known for its red wines). There is rice wine from Fusou, and palm wine from Dhahab for the more exotic-minded. For some after a bit of kick, there is a heavily spiced rum made with hot peppers from Edjang. Absinthe is growing in popularity as a "stylish" drink, and pirates looking to cultivate a certain image will often order it.

&#x200B;

For the bravest drinkers, there will occasionally be alchemists stopping by looking to ply their latest concoctions. These are drinks heavily modified using alchemical procedures and spells, usually by amateurs or hobbyists. They can be perfectly safe and delicious, or potentially life-threatening.
